-- title:
--   Height-one localisations of a ring with crossing-model completion
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian local domain and let $W$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal. Let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, let $E \ge 1$ be a natural number, and suppose given a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R` onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ E)`, that is, onto the quotient of the ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ of formal multivariate power series in two variables by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi^E)$. Suppose further that some $\varpi \in R$ has the property that $\iota$ sends the canonical image of $\varpi$ in the completion to `const (π ^ E) π`, the class of the constant power series $C(\pi)$. Finally let $Q$ be a prime ideal of $R$ with $\varpi \in Q$ and $Q$ distinct from the maximal ideal of $R$. Then the localisation $R_Q$ of $R$ at $Q$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the statement that a two-dimensional Noetherian local domain whose completion is the crossing (ordinary double point) model is normal, so that its localisations at the height-one primes through the node — geometrically the two branches $(\pi, X_0)$ and $(\pi, X_1)$ — are discrete valuation rings. It is used in the analysis of node charts on modular curves, in particular to produce valuation rings in localised node rings and to describe the primes of a node chart other than the node ideal.
